Implementing a multi-tree list (also known as a tree grid or hierarchical data table) in an Angular application involves several steps. Below is a high-level guide on how you can achieve this:

### 1. Setup Your Project

First, ensure you have Node.js and Angular CLI installed.

```bash
npm install -g @angular/cli
ng new your-app-name
cd your-app-name
```

### 2. Create the Tree List Component

Create a component for the tree list using Angular's `@Component` decorator.

```typescript
// src/app/tree-list/tree-list.component.ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import * as d3 from 'd3';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-tree-list',
  templateUrl: './tree-list.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./tree-list.component.css']
})
export class TreeListComponent {
  public treeData: any[] = [];
  public selectedNode: any;

  constructor() {}

  ngOnInit(): void {
    // Initialize the tree structure here
    const root = {
      id: 0,
      children: [
        { id: 1, title: 'Item 1' },
        { id: 2, title: 'Item 2', children: [{ id: 5, title: 'Sub Item 1' }, { id: 6, title: 'Sub Item 2' }] }
      ]
    };

    this.treeData = [root];
  }

  expandNode(node: any): void {
    if (node.children) {
      node.expanded = !node.expanded;
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. HTML Template

Create a template file (`tree-list.component.html`) that uses D3.js to render the tree.

```html
<!-- src/app/tree-list/tree-list.component.html -->
<div id="tree">
  <div id="tree-root" [attr.style]="{ height: `${height}px`, width: `${width}px` }"></div>
</div>

<script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/d3/7.1.4/d3.min.js"></script>
<style>
  #tree-root {
    cursor: pointer;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    background-color: white;
  }
</style>
```

### 4. CSS Styling

Add some basic styling to make it look nice.

```css
/* src/app/tree-list/tree-list.component.css */
#tree-root {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-around;
}

.node {
  cursor: pointer;
  user-select: none;
  padding: 5px;
  font-size: 18px;
  color: #000;
}

.node:hover {
  background-color: #f1f1f1;
}

.selected-node {
  background-color: #ebebeb;
}

.selected-node > div {
  opacity: 0;
}
```

### 5. Update Main App

Update the main app to include the `TreeListComponent`.

```typescript
// src/main.ts
import { platformBrowserDynamic } from '@angular/platform-browser-dynamic';
import { AppModule } from './app/app.module';

platformBrowserDynamic().bootstrapModule(AppModule)
  .catch(err => console.error(err));
```

### 6. Run Your Application

Finally, run your application:

```bash
ng serve
```

Open your browser at http://localhost:4200 to see the multi-tree list working.

